00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
i'm busting my ass trying to keep you alive,dean,

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
and you act like you couldn't care less.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
truth is,i'm tired,sam.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
it's like there's a light at the end of the tunnel.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
it's hellfire,dean.whatever.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
you're my big brother.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
there's nothing i wouldn't do for you.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.579
and i don't care what it takes. i'm gonna get you out of this.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:04.009
well,what can i do for you,sam?

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:05.809
you can let dean out of his deal right now.

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:08.309
i'm just a saleswoman.i got a boss,like everybody.

00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:09.649
he holds the contract.

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:11.879
and who's your boss?i can't tell you.

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:13.649
i'm sorry,sam,

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.079
but there's no way out of this one.

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:44.649
supernatural season 3  episode 6

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:56.649
so,i've been waiting since maple springs.

00:02:56.679 --> 00:02:57.909
you got something to tell me?

00:02:57.949 --> 00:02:59.909
it's not your birthday.

00:02:59.949 --> 00:03:01.349
no.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.709
happy purim?dude,i don't know.

00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:07.149
i have no idea what you're talking --

00:03:07.179 --> 00:03:08.709
there's a bullet missing from the colt.

00:03:08.749 --> 00:03:11.209
you want to tell me how that happened?

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:13.779
i know it wasn't me.

00:03:13.809 --> 00:03:16.509
so unless you were shooting at some incredibly evil cans...

00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:18.579
you went after her,didn't you?the crossroads demon.

00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:20.009
after i told you not to.

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:22.009
yeah,well...

00:03:22.049 --> 00:03:24.379
you could have gotten yourself killed!i didn't.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:25.549
and you shot her.

00:03:25.579 --> 00:03:26.849
she was a smartass.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:31.509
so,what? does that meani'm out of my deal?

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:33.079
don't you think

00:03:33.109 --> 00:03:36.579
i might have mentioned that little fact,dean?

00:03:36.609 --> 00:03:39.579
no. someone else holds the contract.

00:03:39.609 --> 00:03:42.009
- who?
- she wouldn't say.

00:03:45.009 --> 00:03:46.909
well,we should find out who.

00:03:46.949 --> 00:03:50.579
of course,our best lead would be the crossroads demon.

00:03:50.609 --> 00:03:51.909
oh,wait a minute...

00:03:51.949 --> 00:03:54.549
- that's not funny.
- no,it's not!

00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:56.379
it was a stupid freaking risk,and you shouldn't have done it.

00:03:56.409 --> 00:03:57.749
i shouldn't have done it?

00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:59.149
you're my brother,dean.

00:03:59.179 --> 00:04:01.949
and no matter what you do,i'm gonna try and save you.

00:04:01.979 --> 00:04:04.679
and i'm sure as hell not gonnaapologize for it,all right?

00:04:11.249 --> 00:04:13.109
but i don't understand.

00:04:13.149 --> 00:04:16.249
i already went over all this with the other detectives.

00:04:16.279 --> 00:04:17.749
right,yes.

00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:19.779
but,see,we're with the sheriff's department,

00:04:19.809 --> 00:04:22.479
not the police department --different departments.

00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:24.409
so,mrs. case...

00:04:24.449 --> 00:04:28.009
please.ms. case.

00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:33.479
okay.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:37.179
um,ms. case,um...

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:40.109
you were the one who found your niece,correct?

00:04:40.149 --> 00:04:43.079
i came home,she was in the shower.

00:04:43.109 --> 00:04:44.079
drowned?

00:04:44.109 --> 00:04:45.909
so the coroner says.

00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:48.679
now,you tell me,how can someone drown in the shower?

00:04:48.709 --> 00:04:49.949
how would you describe

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:51.909
sheila's behavior in the days before her death?

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:53.909
i mean,did she seem frightened?

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:56.249
maybe she said something out of the ordinary?

00:04:56.279 --> 00:04:58.149
wait a minute.

00:04:58.179 --> 00:05:01.079
you're working with alex,aren't you?

00:05:01.109 --> 00:05:03.949
yep. absolutely.

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:06.279
alex and us,we're like this.

00:05:06.309 --> 00:05:08.979
why didn't you say so?

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:12.349
alex has been such a comfort.

00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:16.309
but i'm sorry.i thought the case was solved.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.109
well,no.no,not yet.

00:05:19.149 --> 00:05:20.549
i see.

00:05:20.579 --> 00:05:22.809
so,anyways,we were talking about your niece.

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:24.379
well,yes.

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:27.479
sheila mentioned something quite strange before she died.

00:05:27.509 --> 00:05:31.379
she said she saw a boat.a boat?

00:05:31.409 --> 00:05:34.179
yes. one minute it was there,then it was gone.

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:36.149
it just disappeared right before her eyes.

00:05:37.809 --> 00:05:40.849
you think it could be a ghost ship?

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:46.179
alex thinks it could be a ghost ship.

00:05:50.009 --> 00:05:52.049
could be.

00:05:54.449 --> 00:05:58.009
you let me know if there's anything else i can do for you.

00:06:06.279 --> 00:06:07.809
anything at all.

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:17.679
what a crazy,old broad.

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:20.179
why? because she believes in ghosts?

00:06:20.209 --> 00:06:22.749
look at you.sticking up for your girlfriend.

00:06:22.779 --> 00:06:24.709
- you cougar hound.
- bite me.

00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:26.279
not if she bites you first.

00:06:26.309 --> 00:06:28.909
so,who's this alex?we got another player in town?

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:31.079
maybe,maybe not.doesn't change our job.

00:06:31.109 --> 00:06:32.849
and what looked like a ghost ship,right?

00:06:32.879 --> 00:06:34.949
it's not the first one sighted around here,either.

00:06:34.979 --> 00:06:37.049
every 37 years,like clockwork,

00:06:37.079 --> 00:06:39.479
reports of a vanishing three-mast clipper ship

00:06:39.509 --> 00:06:40.749
out in the bay.

00:06:40.779 --> 00:06:44.609
and every 37 years,a rash of weirdo,dry-land drownings.

00:06:44.649 --> 00:06:46.979
- so,whatever's happening is just getting started.
- yeah.

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:48.309
what's the lore?

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:50.209
well,there are apparitions of old wrecks

00:06:50.249 --> 00:06:51.649
sighted all over the world.

00:06:51.679 --> 00:06:53.099
the s.s. violet,the griffin

00:06:53.149 --> 00:06:54.349
the flying dutchman

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:56.409
almost all of them are death omens.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:58.609
so,you see the ship and then a few hours later,

00:06:58.649 --> 00:07:00.479
you pucker up and kiss your ass goodbye?

00:07:00.509 --> 00:07:01.509
basically.

00:07:01.549 --> 00:07:02.879
what's the next step?

00:07:02.909 --> 00:07:03.879
i got to i.d. the boat.

00:07:03.909 --> 00:07:05.009
that shouldn't be too hard.

00:07:05.049 --> 00:07:06.779
i mean,how many three-mast clipper ships

00:07:06.809 --> 00:07:07.909
have wrecked off the coast?

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:09.849
i checked that too,actually.

00:07:09.879 --> 00:07:11.709
over 150.

00:07:13.149 --> 00:07:14.749
crap.

00:07:24.549 --> 00:07:26.979
this is where we parked the car,right?

00:07:27.009 --> 00:07:29.409
i thought so.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:32.079
where's my car?

00:07:32.109 --> 00:07:34.309
did you feed the meter?

00:07:34.349 --> 00:07:36.049
yes,i fed the meter.

00:07:36.079 --> 00:07:38.179
sam,where's my car?somebody stole my car!

00:07:38.209 --> 00:07:39.949
calm down.

00:07:39.979 --> 00:07:43.079
i am calmed down!somebody stole my ca--

00:07:44.309 --> 00:07:46.349
oh,my god.

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:47.749
take it easy.

00:07:47.779 --> 00:07:51.509
the '67 impala?was that yours?

00:07:51.549 --> 00:07:52.509
bela

00:07:52.549 --> 00:07:53.849
i'm sorry.

00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:55.849
- i had that car towed.
- you what?!

00:07:55.879 --> 00:07:58.849
- well,it wasin a tow-away zone.
- no,it wasn't!

00:07:58.879 --> 00:08:00.879
it was when i finished with it.

00:08:00.909 --> 00:08:02.849
what the hell are you even doing here?

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:04.449
a little yachting.

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:06.249
you're alex.

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:09.509
you're working with that old lady.

00:08:09.549 --> 00:08:11.049
gert's a dear old friend.

00:08:11.079 --> 00:08:13.049
yeah,right.what's your angle?

00:08:13.079 --> 00:08:14.349
there's no angle.

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:16.849
there's a lot of lovely old women like gert

00:08:16.879 --> 00:08:18.849
up and down the eastern seaboard.

00:08:18.879 --> 00:08:20.279
i sell them charms,

00:08:20.309 --> 00:08:23.109
perform seances so they can commune with their dead cats.

00:08:23.149 --> 00:08:25.349
and let me guess,it's all a con.

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:28.409
the comfort i provide them is very real.

00:08:28.449 --> 00:08:30.409
how do you sleep at night?

00:08:30.449 --> 00:08:33.809
on silk sheets,rolling naked in money.

00:08:35.779 --> 00:08:38.809
really,sam,i'd expect the attitude from him. but you?

00:08:38.849 --> 00:08:40.709
you shot me.

00:08:40.749 --> 00:08:42.279
i barely grazed you.

00:08:44.609 --> 00:08:47.509
cute. but a bit of a drama queen,yeah?

00:08:47.549 --> 00:08:48.909
you do know what's going on around here.

00:08:48.949 --> 00:08:50.649
this ghost-ship thing,it is real.

00:08:50.679 --> 00:08:52.079
i'm aware.

00:08:52.109 --> 00:08:53.729
thanks for telling gert the case wasn't solved

00:08:54.129 --> 00:08:54.679
by the way.

00:08:54.709 --> 00:08:56.079
it isn't.

00:08:56.109 --> 00:08:57.409
she didn't know that.

00:08:57.449 --> 00:08:59.579
now the old bag's stopped payment

00:08:59.609 --> 00:09:01.809
and she's demanding some real answers.

00:09:01.849 --> 00:09:03.249
look...

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:04.439
just stay out of my way

00:09:04.539 --> 00:09:05.979
before you cause any more trouble.

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:09.779
i'd get to that car if i were you...

00:09:09.809 --> 00:09:11.979
before they find the arsenal in the trunk.

00:09:15.309 --> 00:09:16.579
ciao.

00:09:16.609 --> 00:09:20.049
can i shoot her?

00:09:20.079 --> 00:09:21.979
not in public.

00:09:36.949 --> 00:09:38.379
hello?

00:10:25.919 --> 00:10:28.189
police said that he drowned,

00:10:28.219 --> 00:10:29.989
but i don't u-understand how...

00:10:30.019 --> 00:10:32.689
i am so sorry for your loss,mr. warren.

00:10:32.719 --> 00:10:34.549
now,if you could just tell me one more time

00:10:34.589 --> 00:10:35.989
about the ship your brother saw.

00:10:36.019 --> 00:10:38.149
ma'am,i think this man's been through quite enough.

00:10:38.189 --> 00:10:39.789
you should go.

00:10:39.819 --> 00:10:41.289
but i just have a few more questions.

00:10:41.319 --> 00:10:43.389
no,you don't.

00:10:44.889 --> 00:10:47.219
thank you for your time.

00:10:49.619 --> 00:10:52.119
sorry you had to deal with that. they're like roaches.

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:57.819
so,we heard you say your brother saw a ship.

00:10:57.849 --> 00:10:59.389
yeah,that's right.

00:10:59.419 --> 00:11:01.549
did he tell you what it looked like?

00:11:03.349 --> 00:11:07.089
it was,uh... like the old yankee clippers.

00:11:07.119 --> 00:11:08.949
a smuggling vessel.

00:11:08.989 --> 00:11:11.619
the rakish topsail,a barkentine rigging.

00:11:11.649 --> 00:11:13.549
angel figurehead on the bow.

00:11:13.589 --> 00:11:15.849
that's a lot of detail for a ship your brother saw.

00:11:15.889 --> 00:11:18.089
my brother and i were night diving.

00:11:18.119 --> 00:11:19.589
i saw the ship,too.

00:11:21.989 --> 00:11:23.119
excuse me,officers,

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:25.289
i'm not sure those men are detectives.

00:11:26.549 --> 00:11:28.719
all right. well,we'll be in touch.

00:11:28.749 --> 00:11:30.149
thank you.

00:11:34.089 --> 00:11:35.749
i see you got your car back.

00:11:35.789 --> 00:11:37.849
you really want to come near me

00:11:37.889 --> 00:11:40.189
when i got a loaded gun in my hands?

00:11:40.219 --> 00:11:42.489
now,now. mind your blood pressure.

00:11:42.519 --> 00:11:44.189
why are you even still here?

00:11:44.249 --> 00:11:46.419
you have enough to i.d. the boat?

00:11:46.449 --> 00:11:48.589
that guy back there saw the ship.

00:11:48.619 --> 00:11:50.589
yeah? and?

00:11:50.619 --> 00:11:53.989
and he's going to die,so we have to save him.

00:11:54.019 --> 00:11:56.049
how sweet.

00:11:56.089 --> 00:11:58.149
you think this is funny?

00:11:58.189 --> 00:11:59.389
he's cannon fodder.

00:11:59.419 --> 00:12:01.949
he can't be saved in time,and you know it.

00:12:04.119 --> 00:12:07.849
yeah,well,see,we have souls,so we're gonna try.

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:10.989
well,i'm actually gonna find the ship and put an end to this.

00:12:11.019 --> 00:12:12.289
but you have fun.

00:12:16.389 --> 00:12:18.949
hey,bela,how'd you get like this,huh?

00:12:18.989 --> 00:12:22.219
what,did daddy not give you enough hugs or something?

00:12:22.249 --> 00:12:24.689
i don't know. your daddy give you enough?

00:12:26.619 --> 00:12:28.619
don't you dare look down your nose at me.

00:12:28.649 --> 00:12:29.949
you're not better than i am.

00:12:29.989 --> 00:12:32.089
we help people.

00:12:32.119 --> 00:12:33.319
come on.

00:12:33.349 --> 00:12:35.549
you do this out of vengeance and obsession.

00:12:35.589 --> 00:12:38.049
you're a stone's throw from being a serial killer.

00:12:39.119 --> 00:12:41.889
whereas i,on the other hand,

00:12:41.919 --> 00:12:44.289
i get paid to do a job and i do it.

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:46.249
so,you tell me -- which is healthier?

00:12:46.289 --> 00:12:50.789
bela,why don't you just leave? we've got work to do.

00:12:50.819 --> 00:12:52.919
yeah. you're 0 for 2.

00:12:52.949 --> 00:12:54.519
bang-up job so far.

00:13:15.419 --> 00:13:17.119
anything good?

00:13:17.149 --> 00:13:18.889
no. not really.

00:13:18.919 --> 00:13:21.719
i mean,both brothers are duke university grads.

00:13:21.749 --> 00:13:23.889
no criminal record.

00:13:23.919 --> 00:13:26.649
i mean,a few speeding tickets.

00:13:26.689 --> 00:13:29.089
they inherited their father's real estate fortune

00:13:29.119 --> 00:13:30.289
six years ago.

00:13:30.319 --> 00:13:33.289
- how much?
- $112 million.

00:13:33.319 --> 00:13:35.619
nice life.

00:13:35.649 --> 00:13:38.249
yeah. i mean,nice,clean,aboveboard.

00:13:38.289 --> 00:13:41.519
so,why did they see the ship?

00:13:41.549 --> 00:13:43.989
why sheila,too? what do they all have in common?

00:13:44.019 --> 00:13:45.149
maybe nothing.

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:46.549
no. there's always something.

00:13:46.589 --> 00:13:48.349
hey,you!

00:13:48.389 --> 00:13:52.089
i think we've been made.

00:13:52.119 --> 00:13:55.019
what are you guys doing?! you watching me?!

00:13:55.049 --> 00:13:56.519
sir,calm down. please.

00:13:56.549 --> 00:13:58.849
you guys aren't cops!

00:13:58.889 --> 00:14:01.519
not dressed like that. not -- not in that crappy car.

00:14:01.549 --> 00:14:03.119
whoa,hey. no need to get nasty.

00:14:03.149 --> 00:14:04.889
we are cops,okay? we're undercover.

00:14:04.919 --> 00:14:07.019
we're here because we think you're in danger.

00:14:07.049 --> 00:14:08.089
from who?!

00:14:08.119 --> 00:14:10.249
if you just settle down,we'll talk about it.

00:14:10.289 --> 00:14:12.119
look,you guys just stay away from me!

00:14:12.149 --> 00:14:14.049
wait.

00:14:17.249 --> 00:14:19.689
hey,you moron! we're trying to help you!

00:14:29.789 --> 00:14:31.319
- that can't be good.
- no.

00:14:31.349 --> 00:14:33.019
get the salt gun.

00:14:56.589 --> 00:14:57.689
peter!

00:14:59.349 --> 00:15:00.549
sam!

00:15:12.049 --> 00:15:14.549
come on.

00:15:37.989 --> 00:15:39.659
you want to say it,or should i?

00:15:41.959 --> 00:15:43.189
what?

00:15:43.219 --> 00:15:45.189
you can't save everybody,sam.

00:15:47.189 --> 00:15:50.119
yeah,right. so -- so,what? you feel better now or what?

00:15:50.159 --> 00:15:52.559
no. not really.

00:15:52.589 --> 00:15:54.389
me neither.

00:15:57.489 --> 00:15:58.929
you got to under--

00:15:58.959 --> 00:16:01.689
it's just lately i feel like i can't save anybody.

00:16:47.959 --> 00:16:50.559
dear god...

00:16:50.589 --> 00:16:53.119
are you actually squatting?

00:16:53.159 --> 00:16:56.219
charming.

00:16:56.259 --> 00:16:59.419
so,how did things go last night with peter?

00:17:02.519 --> 00:17:03.889
that well,huh?

00:17:03.929 --> 00:17:05.959
if you say "i told you so,"

00:17:05.989 --> 00:17:08.459
i swear to god,i'll start swinging.

00:17:08.489 --> 00:17:11.789
look,i think the three of us should have a heart-to-heart.

00:17:11.819 --> 00:17:14.029
that's assuming you have a heart.

00:17:14.059 --> 00:17:15.889
dean,please.

00:17:15.929 --> 00:17:19.619
i'm sorry about what i said before,okay?

00:17:19.659 --> 00:17:21.759
i come bearing gifts.

00:17:23.189 --> 00:17:24.359
such as?

00:17:24.389 --> 00:17:26.589
i've i.d.'d the ship.

00:17:29.959 --> 00:17:33.719
it's the espirito santo,a merchant sailing vessel.

00:17:33.759 --> 00:17:35.889
quite a colorful history.

00:17:35.929 --> 00:17:38.659
in 1859,a sailor was accused of treason.

00:17:38.689 --> 00:17:41.389
he was tried aboard ship in a kangaroo court and hanged.

00:17:41.419 --> 00:17:42.559
he was 37.

00:17:42.589 --> 00:17:44.889
which would explain the 37-year cycle.

00:17:44.929 --> 00:17:46.359
aren't you a sharp tack?

00:17:46.389 --> 00:17:48.389
there's a photo of him somewhere.

00:17:48.419 --> 00:17:49.659
here.

00:17:51.959 --> 00:17:54.889
isn't that the customer we saw last night?

00:17:54.929 --> 00:17:56.659
